  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 250 AM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nThursday...This could be a day were the rounds of heavy rainfall add \nup and the flooding potential increases especially by late Thu \nnight. After we may have yet another strong to severe MCS or storm \ncluster move acrs the area during the day, there are synoptic scale \nsignals that the LLVL west-to-east boundary gets enhanced and is a \nfocus point of LLJ convergence and moisture feed, fueling more \nthunderstorms possibly in a back-building scenario as Thu night \nprogresses. Where this west-to-east line of convection lays out \nstill uncertain of course at this juncture of the game but CAM \nensembles are hinting along to a county or two north of the I-80 \ncorridor. Depending on what occurs rainfall-wise leading up to this \nscenario, could see the eventual need for a flood watch for Thu or \nThu night.\n\nFriday through Tuesday...Latest ensemble and upper jet trends \nsuggest the upper ridge and heat dome to get presses eastward again \nwith some amplitude thrust up the mid to upper MS RVR Valley with \nwest coast L/W troffiness establishment. This could make for another \nheat and storm track battle zone on Friday for the region, until the \ntrack then gets shunted more to the north acrs MN and WI while we \nheat up again. Still on the southern fringe, couldn't rule out MCS \nseepage down this far south into the local at times over the weekend \nas well. The action may last into early next week with longer range \nsigns of upper ridge dampening and flattening to get us back under \nthe influence of ring of fire periphery.",
